WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.420
- [Host] Meet Wesley.

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.290
He likes carrots.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.453
He spends most of his time sunbathing.

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:10.073
And life is best when he can actually see.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.170
For Wesley's owner and

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:16.640
WSJ executive producer Adam Banicki

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.450
now is passed the time when he'd

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.160
normally take Wesley to the groomer.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.570
- So it's probably been like,

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.570
two and a half three months.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:27.400
Wesley is definitely
overdue for a haircut.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.627
- This is Browser.

00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:29.690
[Joanna] Hey.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:30.930
- [Host] With many groomers closed

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.370
owners are looking at scruffy pups.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.290
- [Joanna] He basically just looks like

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.080
a ball of hair walking in the street.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.370
- [Host] And now, it's up to their owners.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.427
Sort of.

00:00:40.427 --> 00:00:41.260
(barks)

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.780
that's where Gary Angel comes in.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.170
- Yes, yes I do have dogs.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.580
- [Host] He runs My Two Dogs,

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.690
a training and grooming
business in New York.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.870
- I've been grooming now

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.670
for probably eighteen years.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.540
Honestly, a lot can go
wrong with dog grooming if

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:56.770
you don't know what you're doing.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:57.840
- [Host] He's here to guide us through

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.270
how to keep these dogs

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.230
and your pup groomed at home.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:04.389
- I, you know, emphasize extreme caution

00:01:04.389 --> 00:01:06.500
when you're doing anything that

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.810
I'm talking about here.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.007
- [Adam] You ready?

00:01:10.007 --> 00:01:12.770
(sneezes)

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:15.020
- [Joanna] Browser, how do you feel

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.320
about your hair right now?

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.720
- [Gary] Step one, run your hands through

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:21.900
your dogs coat.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.330
What you're looking for is

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.402
any clumps of hair any matting.

00:01:27.402 --> 00:01:30.190
- [Adam] Look at all these little mats.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.420
- [Gary] You know, to get a basic idea

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.820
of what kind of shape the coat is in.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.120
- [Joanna] Yeah, it's
a little bit of a knot.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:41.200
- [Gary] They can cause discomfort and

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.422
in cases where they're not taken care of

00:01:44.422 --> 00:01:46.030
you can get you know,

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:48.160
skin issues underneath the mats.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:49.160
- [Joanna] Let me see just like,

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:50.593
how long the paw.

00:01:51.617 --> 00:01:52.450
Not you buddy,

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:53.283
you very cute.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.210
- Step two trim your dog.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.690
Now you're gonna need your comb

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.610
because you want to comb the area out.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.510
You know, and away from the skin.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.990
And then what I use,

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.760
our little ball tip baby scissors

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.630
and don't use kitchen scissors.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:08.940
What you wanna do with the visor

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.184
is you wanna start about here.

00:02:11.184 --> 00:02:12.270
- [Adam] Look at your little visor!

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.070
- [Gary] And comb it forward like bangs.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:15.903
- [Adam] Good boy.

00:02:15.903 --> 00:02:17.863
- [Gary] The visor will overhang the eyes.

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:21.100
And then once you have the visor down

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.335
you just take your scissors and

00:02:23.335 --> 00:02:28.163
you would just very
carefully just trim around.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:30.650
Once you trim it,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.270
and you can see the dog's eyes stop.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.260
- [Adam] Can you see?

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.740
Can you see the camera?

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:36.950
- With the paws,

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:38.340
what you wanna do is

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.470
you wanna have the paw flat

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.660
on the ground and

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.820
you just wanna kinda follow
the shape of the foot

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.610
you know, when you do it like this

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:47.790
the nails will help to

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.493
keep it away from the foot itself.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.393
- Much better.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:55.760
- [Gary] Step three,

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.350
cleaning the ears.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:58.980
You know, you can use a cotton ball,

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:02.120
you can even use a q-tip
on smaller eared dogs.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.610
If you have a local pet store near you,

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.660
see if they have ear cleaner.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.693
In a pinch,

00:03:08.785 --> 00:03:11.240
I've used it many many
times hydrogen peroxide.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.850
Get the q-tip on the long end,

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:14.320
get it wet with you know,

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.490
your ear cleaner,

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:17.270
your hydrogen peroxide and

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.280
go around the outside of the ear

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.065
and a little bit inside the ear.

00:03:22.065 --> 00:03:23.200
- [Adam] Oh it's been awhile.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.050
- And then go back in and

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.220
wipe around again.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.053
- [Adam] Can you hear better?

00:03:28.053 --> 00:03:30.480
- Once you're done cleaning the ear,

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.110
you wanna take some cotton and

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.390
you wanna stuff it in the dogs ears to

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:36.280
try to keep the water out while

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.573
you're washing your dog.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:41.783
Step four is combing.

00:03:43.922 --> 00:03:46.220
You know, you take your steel comb

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.480
and what you wanna do you wanna follow

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.160
the grain of the dogs hair.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:53.980
And if you hit snags what

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:56.220
I will do is I will put my fingers

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:59.040
in between the skin and the snag and

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.970
try to slightly tease it out.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:04.340
And you're not just
yanking on the dogs hair.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.690
- Look at that fluffy coat.

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:08.830
- Step five,

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:10.030
put your dog in the tub.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:12.260
So what you wanna do,

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:14.310
is you wanna use warm water.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.160
You don't want hot water on your dog.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:19.050
You wanna thoroughly wet your dog.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.143
Make sure your dog is wet to the skin.

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:26.510
You put the shampoo on.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.320
Massage it in and

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.943
work it in really well.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:33.760
Please, do not use human shampoo.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:37.360
Use an all-natural dog shampoo.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.320
- I think I have full sud coverage.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.490
- [Gary] Then what you wanna do is

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.360
you wanna rinse your dog.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.720
When the water starts running clear

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.070
then everything is out.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:49.620
- [Adam] You are totally clean.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:54.020
- Step six, dry.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:57.530
- This is Wesley's
favorite part of bath time.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.250
- Now, I'll be honest with you when

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.440
you're drying your dog at home

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.723
you're probably not gonna get 100% dry.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.060
You wanna try to dry them

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:10.190
as much as you can with a hairdryer.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:13.280
You wanna use it on cool or low heat.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:15.270
And while you're drying

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:17.593
just a nice slow back and forth.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:22.760
And if you can make a starburst pattern

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.650
in your dogs coat because

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.390
then the hair won't tangle up

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:28.160
as you're drying it.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.010
Step seven,

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.212
throw a puppy party.

00:05:30.212 --> 00:05:31.050
- [Adam] Want another one for you?

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.210
- Tell your dog it was wonderful,

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:35.170
it was magnificent and

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:36.760
just make a fuss over them.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:38.331
Say, oh good baby!

00:05:38.331 --> 00:05:39.580
What a good baby!

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.140
Let them know that you know,

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:44.710
grooming isn't a horrible experience.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:45.543
- Good boy.

00:05:45.543 --> 00:05:46.840
That wasn't so bad was it?

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.230
- Put up with it and this is what you get.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:50.913
You get a puppy party.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:56.523
- [Joanna] You think you're
going to the groomer?

